    "summary": "High‑energy Vancouver show with soaring jams and stellar Bird Song",
    "blurb": "The June ’73 P.N.E. Coliseum gig delivers a landmark Bird Song and an epic He’s Gone > Truckin’ > The Other One suite. Jerry’s guitar soars on China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, while Phil’s bass detonates through the marathon jams. A must‑listen for anyone chasing that classic ’73 vibe.",
    "review": "June 22, 1973 at Vancouver's P.N.E. Coliseum finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set eases in with tight renditions of classics like Box of Rain and a beautifully voiced Bird Song that sets the tone for what follows. Once the second set kicks off, the band launches into an unforgettable He’s Gone > Truckin’ > The Other One marathon, highlighted by Phil’s “gold‑colored” bass solo and Jerry’s silky, soaring leads. The China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transition is another high point, featuring one of Jerry’s most expressive lead solos of the era and Keith’s fluid piano work that adds a jazzy sheen. Playin’ In The Band builds into an expansive jam that showcases the group’s tight interplay and relentless energy. Across the night, Bill’s jazz‑inflected drumming underpins every surge while Bob provides rock‑steady rhythm guitar throughout. The soundboard recordings capture all of this with crystalline clarity, making this show a quintessential snapshot of the Dead’s 1973 peak.",
